---
# At the repo root, not in _pages/, because _config.yml gives everything in
# _pages/ `layout: single` — which would wrap this in the site's HTML and it
# would stop being JSON. manifest.json sits out here for the same reason.
# `layout: null` says it again, in case the defaults ever change.
layout: null
permalink: /admin-upkeep.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
=============================================================================
admin-upkeep.json — the "needs a human" list, for the editor to read
=============================================================================
/admin/ fetches this and shows a quiet banner when there is something to do,
so the reminder reaches her where she already is instead of waiting on a page
she has no reason to open.

A COUNT AND A LIST OF NAMES, AND NOTHING ELSE
This file carries no detail, on purpose. Netlify serves static files to anyone
who asks for the URL — a login can only be checked after the file has already
been sent (see _includes/admin-gate.html) — so whatever is written here is
public whether or not the page that reads it is gated. The sentences, which
name what is half-finished about the site, stay on /admin-stats/ behind the
login.

  count    how many things need a hand. Worth nothing to a stranger.
  alerts   one array per thing, holding a short hash for each ROW of it — a
           post with no map pin, a country with no flag — from
           _plugins/upkeep_key.rb. On /admin-stats/ she can set any single row
           aside as fine; that is remembered in the browser under the same
           hash, and both pages share an origin, so the banner can skip an
           alert she has nothing left to do about instead of nagging her about
           it again. Hashed rather than readable precisely because this file
           is public — the hash exists to be compared, never to be read.

Both numbers come from _includes/upkeep-data.html, the same include
/admin-stats/ renders, so the banner and the dashboard cannot disagree.

No layout, and the front matter above is what makes Jekyll run Liquid here.
=============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- include country-data.html -%}
{%- include upkeep-data.html -%}
{
  "generated": {{ site.time | date_to_xmlschema | jsonify }},
  "count": {{ upkeep.size }},
  "alerts": [{% for keys in upkeep_keys %}{% unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{{ keys | split: " " | jsonify }}{% endfor %}]
}
